# Integration tests (CLI + artifacts)

Crate `lovelace_integration_tests` (`lovelace/integration_tests`) builds [samples](../../samples/) with the `lovelace` CLI and checks generated artifacts. Shared helpers live in `Lovelace.Main.Integration_Tests.Support`.

These tests may invoke **optional host tools on PATH**. Do **not** `depends-on`, vendor, or wrap those tools as Alire/crate dependencies (see dependencies rule). CI installs them via `bytecodealliance/actions` (`wasmtime/setup`, `wasm-tools/setup`).

## Preamble

Before any test runs, print tool availability and **require** both tools on `PATH`:

```text
tools:
  wasm-tools  [available] /path/to/wasm-tools
  wasmtime    [available] /path/to/wasmtime
```

Missing either tool fails the suite immediately (integration tests are not meaningful without them).

## Always: build + artifacts

For every sample under test:

1. `lovelace build … --output-format wasm,wat --force`
2. Assert `obj/<Unit>.lir` and `bin/<Unit>.wasm` / `.wat` / `.wit` exist

Discard child **stdout** when spawning `lovelace` / `wasm-tools` / `wasmtime` so `[info]` lines do not flood the suite. Keep **stderr** so `[err]` / `LV#####` diagnostics still appear.

## Validate (every generated `.wasm` / `.wat`)

```text
wasm-tools validate <file.wasm>
wasm-tools validate <file.wat>
```

Run validation on **every** generated component artifact (programs and modules).

## Run (entrypoint / program only)

Only units with an **entrypoint** (today: `program` compilation units that emit `wasi:cli/run`) are executed after validate.

Modules with no entrypoint are **never** run.

### Host selection (future; today always wasmtime for programs)

| Flavor / target | Runner |
| --- | --- |
| **WASI** | `wasmtime` CLI |
| **native** | `lovelace` CLI (host embedder / JIT) |
| **web** | headless Chrome or Node with the JS glue libraries |

**For the time being**, invoke `wasmtime run -Sp3 -W component-model-async=y` on both `.wasm` and `.wat` for program samples.

## Per-test reporting

Each test prints one status line (AUnit success chatter is suppressed):

```text
support locate and compose           [OK]
build validate and run Hello         [OK]
build and validate modules           [OK]
```

Use `[FAIL]` on assertion failure and `[INCONCLUSIVE]` only when a tool step is unexpectedly missing after the preamble.

## Support API

Prefer `Integration_Tests.Support` for locate/build/assert/validate/run/report so fixtures stay thin:

- `Report_And_Require_Tools` — `wasm-tools` / `wasmtime` as status lines (`[OK]`/`[FAIL]`), then assert both on PATH
- `Report_Test_Result` — `NAME [OK|FAIL|INCONCLUSIVE]` (OK green, FAIL red, INCONCLUSIVE gray via `Lovelace.Test_Status`)
- Suite harness prints a cyan `Report_Suite_Header` before tool checks and fixtures
- `Validate_Unit_Artifacts` / `Run_Unit_Entrypoint`
- `Tool_Status` — `Missing` | `Succeeded` | `Failed`
